# Eval and suggestions

Criteria and section lists come from `getDocumentType(type)`, not a hardcoded
DMAIC array. Investigation criteria in `criteria.ts` include **conclusion**.
DV mixes LLM criteria with deterministic `check()` functions.

## Eval

- Entry: `evaluateSection()` in `src/lib/ai/evaluate.ts`.
- Cache hash: `evaluationContentHash()` — section content + `dependsOn`
  sections + `promptVersion`. Bump `prompts.promptVersion` (investigation:
  `PROMPT_VERSION` in `section-prompts.ts`) or stale evals will not rerun.
- Placeholders: `capEvaluationStatusForPlaceholders()` — never `not_met`
  solely for unfilled placeholders.
- Report AI Check (`POST .../evaluate`) walks `getEvaluatableSections()` for
  the report's document type. Do not hardcode DMAIC.

## Suggestions

- Entry: `generateSuggestionsForSection()`. Gate ≡ apply via
  `probeRichEdit` / `probePlainEdit` in `src/lib/suggestions/locator.ts`.
- Canonical anchor text is `flattenForAnchor` — no markdown pipes.
- Accept/dismiss: three-way merge when `suggestionBase`/`suggestionIntent`
  are stored (`mergeField` in `three-way-merge.ts`); otherwise locate the
  frozen span. If merge reports identity but the stored delete/insert still
  locates and the insert is not already in the field, preview and apply that
  span — do not hide inline marks behind "already in the document." PATCH
  section → flip comment. Never resolve without a successful apply. Zero-ops
  dismiss (`already_present`), not resolve. A superseded sibling is
  `dismissed` with `resolutionReason: "superseded_by:<id>"`, never `resolved`.
- Bulk apply re-merges each open suggestion against the in-memory doc.
  Overlapping edits in a section apply recursively; non-overlapping edits
  persist as one section PATCH. Preview applied wording before that PATCH
  so insert text does not vanish during save. Range-contained siblings are
  dismissed, not applied into an overwrite. Locate failures stay open; the
  toast reports them. Do not dismiss a skip — that is a silent failure.
- `draft_field` refuses a filled field unless `replaceFilledField: true`.
  After a redraft, filled `[Label: value]` placeholders must be preserved
  unless the caller opted into replacing them.
- Same-turn `propose_edit` cards (Document and Agent chrome) fold when
  locatable ranges sit within `COALESCING_GAP` (20) characters. There is
  no max-cards budget. Do not fold lead-ins, tables, figures, citation
  splits, or cells.
- Bump `SUGGEST_PROMPT_VERSION` when the suggestion prompt changes.
  Bump `CHAT_PROMPT_VERSION` when chat edit-tool copy changes.
- Whole-field is derived: planned operations cover every merge block
  (`operationsCoverWholeField`), plus `ai_redraft`. Coverage classifies
  edit vs rewrite; `propose_edit` does not refuse large spans.
